From: nuubOS <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] spnego: keep running without a Kerberos keytab

With Kerberos support built in (libkrb5 is in the image for another
package) ksmbd.mountd aborts its worker when no keytab exists, and the
manager restarts it every second forever (CPU and battery, a kernel
"Reconnect to a new user space daemon" message each time). Disable the
Kerberos mechanisms instead; NTLMSSP password logins are unaffected.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/tools/management/spnego.c
+++ b/tools/management/spnego.c
@@ -58,10 +58,16 @@
 		mech_ctx->params.krb5.keytab_name =
 			g_strdup(global_conf.krb5_keytab_file);
 
+	/* Without a keytab Kerberos cannot work: leave the mechanism out
+	 * (NTLMSSP still authenticates) instead of aborting the worker, which
+	 * the manager would restart every second forever. */
 	for (i = 0; i < SPNEGO_MAX_MECHS; i++)
 		if (mech_ctxs[i].ops->setup &&
-		    mech_ctxs[i].ops->setup(&mech_ctxs[i]))
-			abort();
+		    mech_ctxs[i].ops->setup(&mech_ctxs[i])) {
+			pr_info("Kerberos unavailable, SPNEGO mechanism %d disabled\n", i);
+			mech_ctxs[i].ops->cleanup(&mech_ctxs[i]);
+			mech_ctxs[i].ops = NULL;
+		}
 }
 
 void spnego_destroy(void)
@@ -320,7 +326,7 @@
 	}
 
 	mech_ctx = get_mech(mech_type);
-	if (!mech_ctx) {
+	if (!mech_ctx || !mech_ctx->ops) {
 		retval = -ENOTSUP;
 		pr_info("No support for Kerberos 5\n");
 		goto out;
